WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.000
Install Aggrega with one command, on
Linux, macOS or Windows.

2
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.800
Ready.

3
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.470
Aggrega works with your AI assistant:

4
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.720
here Claude Code, connected to the
Aggrega MCP server.

5
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.570
One request: turn a LangGraph agent into
an Aggrega workspace

6
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.370
with PostgreSQL memory, for Docker
Compose and Kubernetes.

7
00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:37.170
The assistant drafts the files,
validates them and builds them,

8
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.820
using Aggrega's tools.

9
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.420
The build passes: an Aggregate says
what runs, a Release where,

10
00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.320
a Manifest how. All plain YAML.

11
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.100
In VS Code, the Aggrega extension draws
the workspace as a graph.

12
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:03.150
One workspace, more than one target.
Run it with Docker Compose…

13
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.850
…and the agent answers from a local model.

14
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.500
Build the same workspace for Kubernetes,
and you get its manifests.

15
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.100
Everything is documented…

16
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.200
…and the catalog holds ready-made
components to build on.

17
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:30.100
Get started: one command on
Linux, macOS or Windows.

